hadiths[14]{hadithnumber,text}:
"901","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If livestock injure someone, there is no blood money for them; if someone falls into a well, there is no blood money; if someone falls into a mine, there is no blood money; and there is a fifth share in buried treasure."""
"902","Hasan (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""There is no blood money for an injury caused by an animal, if someone falls into a well there is no blood money for that, if someone is buried under a mine there is no blood money for that, and there is a fifth share in buried treasures."""
"903","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: (similar to the previous hadith)."
"904","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever peeps into someone’s house without permission and they gouge out his eye, there is neither blood money nor retribution for it."""
"905","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever accuses his slave of something, while the slave is innocent of that accusation, then the legal punishment (hadd) will be established upon him, unless the slave is exactly as he has said."""
"906","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever accuses his slave of something while he is innocent of that accusation, then on the Day of Resurrection, the prescribed punishment will be established upon him."""
"907","Umayyah bin Yazid al-Shami narrated, the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever introduces a new practice in Islam, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all the people; on the Day of Resurrection, neither any voluntary nor any obligatory act will be accepted from him."" It was asked: O Messenger of Allah! What is meant by 'hadath'? He (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever kills a soul unjustly or takes revenge without retribution, or invents an innovation without Sunnah."" He said: The meaning of «العدل» is: ransom, and the meaning of «الصرف» is: repentance."
"908","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""If you see anyone committing an evil act (a lustful act) with an animal, then kill that person and the animal. And if you see anyone committing the act of the people of Lot, then kill both the one who does it and the one to whom it is done (the active and the passive participant)."""
"909","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""If a mukatab (a slave with a contract of manumission) is killed, the blood money for the portion he has paid for his freedom will be given as that of a free man, and for the portion he remains a slave, the blood money will be given as that of a slave."""
"910","Yahya bin Kathir narrated from Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) and Marwan bin Al-Hakam a similar narration."
"911","Ikrimah narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) the same narration."
"912","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) gave a verdict regarding the blood money of «مکاتب» that if he is killed, then whatever portion of his «مکاتبة» he has paid, that much of him is considered free, and the remainder will be considered the blood money of a slave."
"913","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: “The blood money for «مکاتب» (if he is killed) will be equal to the amount he has paid for «مکاتبة» .”"
"914","Ikrimah narrated from Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) the same narration, but he did not narrate it as marfu'."
